{
  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-63",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Read the source-plotted function f on its stated bounded domain; retain half-unit cells, solid curve and axis values without adding a query line, a formula or answer annotation.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-63.png",
      "sha256": "5851dbdcb4c4d355c8beab506abd24c7cfc8127e05628a1c7ef3eff7561f0fd0"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-ex",
        "exercise": "938",
        "text": "938. 函数$f$由图象给出（图63），它的定义域是区间$[-1,6]$。利用图象求命题为真的集合（说出回答的理由）：\na) $f(x)=2.5$；\nb) $f(x)<2.5$；\nc) $f(x)>2.5$。"
      }
    ],
    "inventory": [
      {
        "id": "single-source-grid",
        "description": "One shared rectangular lattice with 19 vertical lines and 13 horizontal lines: 18 columns by 12 rows, step 0.5 on both axes, zero phase; x runs -1.5..7.5, y runs -2..4. Grid line gaps around printed axis values and small scan breaks are typography/damage, not missing cells. Rectification of scanning skew is modern.",
        "objects": [
          "source-half-unit-grid"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "source-grid-18-by-12"
        ],
        "requires": [
          "gridDimensions"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "source-axes-and-labels",
        "description": "Horizontal x and vertical y cross at the sole printed origin 0 and point in the positive directions. Printed x values: [-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]; printed y values: -1, 1, 2, 3. There are no printed half-unit values, curve-name labels, point letters or units. Modern labels are offset to keep clear of strokes; for g, nonnegative x values move above their unchanged tick positions so the descending curve cannot obscure them. This side change is modern, not a source label-placement fact.",
        "objects": [
          "source-x-axis",
          "source-y-axis",
